> @copilot+claude-sonnet-4.6 while I was able to verify that this PR indeed allows display mode switching at runtime, the biggest issue is with GUI component scaling: When initializing the GUI component...

Addressed in commit `1869a6a`.

Added `Screen.onResolutionChanged(Dimension)` — the default implementation resizes the screen container to the new window dimensions automatically. Game developers can override this method to also re-layout or rescale their child GUI components:

```java
@Override
public void onResolutionChanged(Dimension newResolution) {
    super.onResolutionChanged(newResolution); // resizes the screen itself
    // re-layout child components relative to the new size
    myButton.setLocation(newResolution.getWidth() / 2 - 100, newResolution.getHeight() / 2);
}
```

`ScreenManager` now registers a `ResolutionChangedListener` on the first `add()` call and forwards all subsequent resolution changes to every registered screen, so the hook is called automatically whenever the window is resized (including after a `DisplayMode` switch).
